{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1261 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "c7f4858cd3e63d7271d8918e9ed973c964fc672d0f85d72931eec292aa43553b" :edb/db-before-t 1260 :edb/db-after-t 1261 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534573 50 #inst "2026-10-12T03:28:05.361Z" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186073486 1074 "We have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$\n\non the left and\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$\n\non the right.\n\n![](images/78/785deacac749a6ed43e5e6a2638677e8ff9e9b58087cb4e471ea85fd50609ce6.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $2$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $2$ times larger than the shaded part on the right.\n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 2 = \\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$" 13194139534573 17592186045417 false] [17592186073486 1074 "We have $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/78/785deacac749a6ed43e5e6a2638677e8ff9e9b58087cb4e471ea85fd50609ce6.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $2$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $2$ times larger than the shaded part on the right.\n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 2 = \\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186073487 1074 "We have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$\n\non the left and\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{15}\n$$\n\non the right.\n\n![](images/ed/ed5517a9242aed1c5b521ca07772dacbb7c96a73c69d4d9c6214a098742358e2.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $5$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $5$ times larger than the shaded part on the right.\n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} \\div {\\color{blue}{5}} = \\dfrac{1}{15}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}5$." 13194139534573 17592186045417 false] [17592186073487 1074 "We have $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{1}{15}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/ed/ed5517a9242aed1c5b521ca07772dacbb7c96a73c69d4d9c6214a098742358e2.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $5$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $5$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} \\div {\\color{blue}{5}} = \\dfrac{1}{15}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}5.$" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186073488 1074 "Notice that in the model, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$\n\non the left.\n\nSince we need to divide by $\\color{blue}3$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/30/30f9bbc604d35a9a15e1418c0cf80eca87fe4d704287c15fb8de7426eb9e3de9.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{9}\n$$\n\nof the whole.\n\nSo, the missing picture is:\n\n![](images/95/951a4bc0607c53aa0c5ed9cebe664b630acf226a6f9844fd9d1b8e6ae952d0ed.png)" 13194139534573 17592186045417 false] [17592186073488 1074 "Notice that in the model, we have $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to divide by $\\color{blue}3$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/30/30f9bbc604d35a9a15e1418c0cf80eca87fe4d704287c15fb8de7426eb9e3de9.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ of the whole.\n\nSo, the missing picture is:\n\n![](images/95/951a4bc0607c53aa0c5ed9cebe664b630acf226a6f9844fd9d1b8e6ae952d0ed.png)" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186073489 1071 "Use the model below to calculate $\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 4$.\n\n![](images/8e/8eccf163bffabb43593188590a1f995544f3d1ac0aebcdd87dce638b230f8165.png)" 13194139534573 17592186045417 false] [17592186073489 1071 "Use the model below to calculate $\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 4.$\n\n![](images/8e/8eccf163bffabb43593188590a1f995544f3d1ac0aebcdd87dce638b230f8165.png)" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186073489 1074 "Since we need to divide by $\\color{blue}4$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}4$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/a3/a34a3fb198ef2ea79f8baf8f0acbdbdc179c6259c614824315d3d96e5ea4e921.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{16}\n$$\n\nof the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 4 = \\dfrac{1}{16}\\,\n$$" 13194139534573 17592186045417 false] [17592186073489 1074 "Since we need to divide by $\\color{blue}4$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}4$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/a3/a34a3fb198ef2ea79f8baf8f0acbdbdc179c6259c614824315d3d96e5ea4e921.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{1}{16}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 4 = \\dfrac{1}{16}\\,.\n$$" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186073716 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426220 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186073716 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426221 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186073717 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426218 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186073717 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426219 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186073718 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426215 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186073718 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426216 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186073719 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426214 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186073719 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426217 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186073948 1050 420.0 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186075052 1064 "Remember that a *unit* fraction is a fraction containing ![](images/cc/ccee5f5be0445cce59832a3def74f395a7d05cc12dc630fb36baf8f3d2d448bd.svg) in the numerator. So, for example, the fractions \n\n![](images/2e/2e38b15a8f3be74e15b87e81264b66571e593de7250dc902aeaa0e7bc1c506bf.svg)\nare both unit fractions, whereas \n\n![](images/d1/d157ce836a54214740d295f545d4c94d8c57d54d92ac7f075ed9b92556c932b1.svg)\nare *not* unit fractions.\n\nIn this lesson, we will use models to divide unit fractions by whole numbers. \n\nLet's use a fraction model to find the value of \n\n![](images/d8/d8815c6716e962ce4aebee24d004d4c591a1bc35c5fdebcd87d26ace61ead7fb.svg)\nWe start with a square model of ![](images/9f/9fcebe90d169f37bbdbf55f9e4ac86ceaf6ea6d573d101f382a12008bb0c5c2a.svg) split *vertically*.\n\n![](images/cc/ccfe0f457342c456200c98cfc46e63bdc1153698282085164eeafae5c2092c45.png)\n\nTo divide ![](images/9a/9ae11798da63cafee6ce5ccf824a7b96f9f7407a4ee445d1431d907c36f5dd1b.svg) by ![](images/db/dbfe30ca4e672459c180bd90f25f84f025162b8ce73260773fb1fbdf39b0a052.svg) we split the above whole into ![](images/6f/6f33d8df0d08ae9bddce540bedf62f46e93e748e4a5b6fd85b1dc626953e44a6.svg) equal parts *horizontally*. Then, we remove any shaded parts that are not in the bottom row.\n\n![](images/79/7940073ba05d3136ee1d465530a60bc3624b7aa06fd7484d30797758a28976d7.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents ![](images/42/42accbcb8cbfd14800ac4a27bc87d5ba529ff4173a91499f32705cd41b0c88b0.svg) of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n![](images/f1/f14a0f0f9efb98bdfe6cf40f4b1bbb2c88dc20272caaf9d604fcc44bce79d53c.svg)" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186075052 1064 "Remember that a *unit* fraction is a fraction containing ${\\color{blue}{1}}$ in the numerator. So, for example, the fractions\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}{1}}2, \\qquad\\dfrac{\\color{blue}{1}}{12}\n$$\n\nare both unit fractions, whereas\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{red}{2}}9, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\color{red}{3}}{5}\n$$\n\nare *not* unit fractions\n\nIn this lesson, we will use models to divide unit fractions by whole numbers.\n\nLet's use a fraction model to find the value of\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2} \\div 2\n$$\n\nWe start with a square model of\n\n$$\n\\dfrac12\n$$\n\nsplit *vertically*.\n\n![](images/cc/ccfe0f457342c456200c98cfc46e63bdc1153698282085164eeafae5c2092c45.png)\n\nTo divide\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nby ${\\color{blue}2}$, we split the above whole into $\\color{blue}2$ equal parts *horizontally*. Then, we remove any shaded parts that are not in the bottom row.\n\n![](images/79/7940073ba05d3136ee1d465530a60bc3624b7aa06fd7484d30797758a28976d7.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nof the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2} \\div 2 = \\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$" 13194139534573 17592186045417 false] [17592186426174 1080 "images/2d/2db872fb5fb0fcd14995cd17d624a4d6548f2599f06fa87751c3f523a4343bd3.png" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186426174 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186426174 1083 #uuid "13decac2-cb86-55aa-808f-d37c3846c461" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186426175 1080 "4" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186426175 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186426175 1083 #uuid "24789ef8-39e5-5eb7-8a31-b15bbcaa8124" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186426176 1080 "\\frac{3}{12}" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186426176 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186426176 1083 #uuid "282af08e-d6ca-5ae5-a8a3-7b9303a4e97d" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186426177 1080 "images/57/5728a31bada1e61de52cb517941554be27bc63670d6fe98ba5c3eda4c2f5d7a4.png" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186426177 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186426177 1083 #uuid "37313ebf-b581-5895-b409-a88ec4b3323b" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186426178 1080 "7" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186426178 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186426178 1083 #uuid "3d8eb349-8d81-5b23-8b12-380de2e96e35" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186426179 1080 "images/12/12af273d7c64a18f27ba95e0a2aa624cb74ab3ef2e6777349d53b09a721e6754.png" 13194139534573 17592186045417 true] [17592186426179 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139534573 17592186045417 true]